[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3454022669","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112075#issuecomment-3454022669","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112075","id":3454022669,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7N4DQN","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-28T01:18:37Z","updated_at":"2025-10-28T01:18:37Z","body":"This may also make using `tween_subtween()` more efficient. Currently, even if you know you're going to be making a tween as a subtween, you still have to initially add it to the tree with `create_tween()`, and then the `tween_subtween()` call later removes it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3454022669/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3454029821","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112075#issuecomment-3454029821","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112075","id":3454029821,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7N4E_9","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-28T01:22:25Z","updated_at":"2025-10-28T01:24:29Z","body":"@Meorge with this pr it still creates an invalid Tween aka it cannot have Tweeners appended. It's in the same state as a regular Tween which has finished tweening and the tree cleans it up so that ```is_valid()``` returns false.\r\n\r\nAlthough I do think that it would be nice if tweens were more re-usable and there essentially weren't invalid tweens at all.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3454029821/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3454061512","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112075#issuecomment-3454061512","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112075","id":3454061512,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7N4MvI","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-28T01:31:51Z","updated_at":"2025-10-28T01:31:51Z","body":"Ah ok, thank you for the correction!\r\n\r\nIn that case I might be a little worried about allowing the use of the `Tween.new()` constructor directly, as (at least to me) it implies it's ready to have tweeners added to it, similar to the result of `create_tween()`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3454061512/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3454116357","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112075#issuecomment-3454116357","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112075","id":3454116357,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7N4aIF","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-28T01:56:35Z","updated_at":"2025-10-28T01:56:35Z","body":"@Meorge My problem with that is if you try to append tweeners it will give you an error anyways saying that the tween may have been created outside of the scene tree and the docs also clearly state that using ```Tween.new()``` creates an invalid tween.\r\n\r\nAdditionally it would be trivial for me to make it directly say it was created with ```Tween.new()``` upon trying to append a tweener if it needs to be even more clear to the user.\r\n\r\nSo to actively prevent the user from initializing a variable with ```Tween.new()``` by printing an error which has no side effect is a bit ridiculous in my opinion.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3454116357/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]